{
	title: 'Providers see one native tool with versioned READ/EDIT and HELP',
	spec: "Providers see one native tool, tool { cmd: string }. Its cmd text is NAME, an optional /* purpose */ comment, then arguments: JS string literals or ASON objects. Each tools/ module declares its call syntax (Tool.syntax: positional fields, summary, usage) next to its definition; native-tool.ts resolves call text to the module call, and SYSTEM.md's $tools_summary lists enabled modules from the registry. HELP <TOOL> renders precise help from the module's own definition, never a parallel dictionary. A malformed call fails as a tool error naming the problem and the raw text; nothing runs. History stores the resolved call plus the original text; replay sends providers the cmd text (older native calls as NAME { fields }). READ of a text file returns numbered lines and a whole-file version path@hash; EDIT takes path@hash and {range, lines} blocks, applied atomically in one write; a stale hash writes nothing and shows the current lines around each range. EDIT records file changes like bash modifies. BASH keeps background, unsafeToStop, modifies and approval. SYSTEM.md supports $name and ${name} variables.",
	status: 'done',
